{
  "requirement": "The harness instructs the model to finish by calling\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.submission.mcp`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has one obligation: the harness instructs the model to finish by calling `submit_result`. The `submission.mcp` requirement is only cited, so the subject doesn't require its tool shape, schema or acceptance behavior to be tested here. Those are covered by their own requirements.\n\nThree marked tests assert the instruction text in the request the model receives:\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport]` captures the real HTTP request bodies on a local transport. For every request it asserts `input.contains(\"Finish by calling submit_result\")`. This covers both the first turn and the follow-up turn that carries tool output.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat]` asserts that the serialized `messages` of both native-chat requests contain \"Finish by calling submit_result\".\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results]` asserts that the first request's `chat_history` contains \"Finish by calling submit_result\". It also checks the reminder turn.\n\nThe instruction is therefore checked on the provider-agnostic request and on both concrete backends. Each assertion would fail if the instruction were dropped or didn't name `submit_result`.\n\nThe other marked tests, `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` and `typed_submission_references_resolve_and_invalid_results_are_agent_errors`, exercise the submit tool and its schema. The requirement doesn't ask for those checks, and they add no obligation here. I found no gap.",
